# Accepted findings for `trivy config infra/terraform` (personal-scale project; revisit for production use).
#
# AWS-0132 (HIGH)  S3 buckets use SSE-S3 rather than a customer-managed KMS key. Data is low sensitivity
#                  (transient CSV uploads, public SPA assets); SSE-S3 avoids KMS cost/key-policy coupling
#                  with CloudFront OAC and presigned uploads.
AWS-0132
# AWS-0011 (HIGH)  No WAF on CloudFront. Static SPA only; API Gateway has route throttling. WAF adds fixed cost.
AWS-0011
# AWS-0090 (MEDIUM) No S3 versioning: imports are transient (30-day expiry), web bucket is a rebuildable artifact.
AWS-0090
# LOW findings:
# AWS-0017 CloudWatch log groups use the default CloudWatch Logs encryption (no CMK).
AWS-0017
# AWS-0025 DynamoDB uses the AWS managed aws/dynamodb key (SSE on) rather than a CMK.
AWS-0025
# AWS-0089 The shared access-logs bucket does not log to itself (it is the logging target).
AWS-0089
